## Approach

The **Composite Graph API** is the right tool here: each graph is a **unit of work** — all records in a graph (Account + Opportunity) commit atomically, and graphs commit independently, so a failed order never blocks the others. The Account upsert uses the external ID in the URL (`PATCH .../Account/Customer_Number__c/C-1001`), and the Opportunity references the upsert result via `@{acct_1001.id}`. Reference IDs (`acct_1001`, `opp_1001`) are echoed back in the response so the middleware can match results.

```http
POST /services/data/v60.0/composite/graph HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "graphs": [
    {
      "graphId": "SO-1001",
      "compositeRequest": [
        {
          "method": "PATCH",
          "url": "/services/data/v60.0/sobjects/Account/Customer_Number__c/C-1001",
          "referenceId": "acct_1001",
          "body": {
            "Name": "Alder Creek Cafe"
          }
        },
        {
          "method": "POST",
          "url": "/services/data/v60.0/sobjects/Opportunity",
          "referenceId": "opp_1001",
          "body": {
            "Name": "Web order SO-1001",
            "StageName": "Closed Won",
            "CloseDate": "2026-09-26",
            "Amount": 1250,
            "AccountId": "@{acct_1001.id}"
          }
        }
      ]
